"""Amount-specific recurring investigation instructions, separate from cells."""

AMOUNT_TASK = """Determine which reported molecular amounts describe the preparations or arms relevant to the assigned experiment. Identify the actual molecule, construct, preparation or stock, measurement method, reported amount basis and condition for each quantity before nominating numerical and unit spans. Preserve unknown meanings rather than completing them from a nearby protein name. A public searchable name is not required: source-backed experimental relationships can identify the relevant preparations. Distinguish mass concentration from molar concentration, estimated target protein from total protein, and nominal recipe amount from measured active concentration.

For estimates of target and total protein in one stock, identify which estimate belongs in the numerator and which in the denominator, and retain the methods and source passages establishing that they describe the same stock. Target protein and total protein are deliberately different measurands; their difference is not automatically measurement-method disagreement or error. Their ratio is a target/total protein mass-fraction estimate under those methods and the same-stock relationship. It can inform protein-mass purity when the measurands and calibration support that interpretation; it is never automatically validated purity, active fraction, contaminant activity or reliability. Their comparison can also describe a conditional change of mass denominator. Estimates can yield a target/total ratio above one. Preserve potentially inconsistent estimates and their limitations without clamping them. Preserve negative or noisy reported estimates too, without treating a nonpositive mass ratio as a usable physical denominator conversion.

For nominal molar amounts in different experimental arms, identify both actual molecules and preparations, the experiment connecting those arms and the deliberately changed variable. Their amount difference can qualify how comparable the arms are outside that intended change. It does not establish an amount-response correction, equal active sites or isolation of the measured effect. Replacement across vessels does not establish the purity of either preparation. Keep experimental comparability separate from effect isolation.

Nominate exact original number and unit spans; deterministic operations parse, validate, convert supported units and perform arithmetic. Preserve inequalities and approximation, including prose that qualifies an estimate without sitting immediately next to its number. Reported point means a point-form source report, not an exact physical measurement. A reported-point selection cannot override a lexical limit or approximation; unresolved qualification stays unknown. Do not infer a molecular weight, reaction volume, source denominator or stock relationship from matching units. A missing comparison relationship does not erase an individually reported value.

Preserve reported uncertainty and physical observation identity. An approximate estimate is not a standard error, and SD, SEM, confidence intervals and untyped spreads retain their own meanings. Repeated representations and shared observations are not independent measurements. Supply a retained covariance source only when its actual quantities, units and ordered owners apply; missing covariance stays unknown. Do not compose numerical covariance or assume zero dependence to complete a requested cell. Estimated variance is not known variance.

Before any later use of a mass-denominator factor, establish that the saved rate uses this actual stock and total protein mass as its denominator. An already target-normalized rate must not receive the conversion again. The present amount operation retains this conditional relationship without inventing a rate or an activity correction. Return only the parent's requested typed information, with these scientific qualifications. Target correspondence and combined annotation credit remain separate work."""

